WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
(pensive music)

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.370
- [Narrator] This Ukrainian crew

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.400
is driving a British Challenger 2 tank.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.751
Kyiv's forces are training to maneuver,

00:00:07.751 --> 00:00:08.610
(gun loading)

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.780
load ammunition and maintain
Western military vehicles ahead

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.400
of their delivery to the battlefield,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.773
which the UK says could be weeks away.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.650
So far in the war, both Ukraine

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.140
and Russia have been
using Soviet era tanks,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.130
such as the T-72, but the UK
is one of several NATO members

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.500
including Germany and
the US that have offered

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.500
to send Western style tanks to Kyiv.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.930
The Wall Street Journal
visited the Ukrainian troops

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.850
learning to operate
the systems to find out

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.493
the key technical differences
with Russian tanks.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:42.653
- [Trainer] Reverse.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.154
Keep the grips in.

00:00:45.154 --> 00:00:46.887
(tank rumbling)

00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:47.850
- [Narrator] The British Army

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.410
is taking the Ukrainian soldiers

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.510
through different stages of training.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.360
They're currently three
weeks into the program.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.070
First, let's look at maneuvering.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.230
Some drills are being
taught on training tanks,

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.790
which don't have turrets.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.127
- We are at the point
of the advanced sections

00:01:03.127 --> 00:01:06.360
and that's more how to use the tank

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.580
in a tactical environment,
how fast you can move it,

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.070
how much it can take essentially

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.920
before you have to basically
rein it in a little bit.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.570
- [[Narrator] Gregor
is a Ukrainian Soldier

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:16.863
learning these skills.

00:01:17.982 --> 00:01:22.482
(Gregor speaking in foreign language)

00:01:24.358 --> 00:01:26.490
(tank rumbling)

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.290
- [Narrator] The Challenger
2 tanks are slower

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.010
than the Soviet era T-72
vehicles, as they're heavier.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:35.100
- Soviet era tanks are smaller and lighter

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.170
than Western tanks

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:42.170
so they'll find it easier
to get up a steep hill

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.090
because they weigh 45 or 50 tons

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:48.690
as opposed to about 70
tons of a Challenger.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.550
- [Trainer] So when
you've got steep hills,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.860
because the gun might dig into the floor

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.480
when you come down the hill,

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.610
sometimes you'll need
to stop and put the gun

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.223
over the side just to get down the hill.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.720
- [Narrator] Then there's
the differences in firepower.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.180
The Challenger 2 has a 120 millimeter

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.890
rifled barrel tank gun.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.530
That means the inside of
the turret has grooves

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.980
while the T-72 uses what's
known as a smooth bore armament

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.650
which means it has a flat interior.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:21.630
- In theory, rifling makes
the gun more accurate

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.630
but it also slightly slows down the round.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.540
The T-72 has an auto loader

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.270
so there's a sort of circular cassette

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:33.030
of ammunition in the base of the turret.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.140
- [Narrator] That's in contrast

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.930
to the Challenger 2, which
requires manual loading.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.830
- There are four people who
operate a Challenger 2 tank.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.980
We have a loader operator,
which is different

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.960
from the the tanks that
they have at the moment

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.090
because they have an auto
loader in their tanks

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.530
and we have a person to do that.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.840
- [Narrator] The British Army
is training Ukrainian forces

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.240
to load the ammunition
using a simulator machine

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.210
called a loaders drill trainer or LDT.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.670
This helps the crew practice
loading up the tank,

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:00.856
ready to fire.

00:03:00.856 --> 00:03:02.507
(gun shooting)
- [Announcer] target.

00:03:02.507 --> 00:03:03.753
Target stopped.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.790
- The loader needs to
know how to get the big,

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:13.790
heavy 120 millimeter shell
into the breach of the gun.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.900
Now, that just needs practice.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.000
It's not a complicated task

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.100
but physically, it's quite challenging

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.890
and it's even more challenging
when the vehicle's in combat

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:23.973
and moving around.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.510
- [Narrator] Ukrainian
forces are also learning

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.960
to maintain the vehicle
so they can run smoothly.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.210
- We started off with
the maintenance phase

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.490
and the technical details
phase, to install components

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:39.510
how they work, every single
aspect of the tank essentially.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.830
- [Narrator] Lessons include how to check

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.380
these rubber triangles
situated on the wheels.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.393
They need regular checks during combat.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:50.850
- Tracked vehicles do
break down more frequently

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:54.364
than a wheeled vehicle of similar size.

00:03:54.364 --> 00:03:56.280
(pensive music)

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.530
- [Narrator] Overall, military
analysts say the readiness

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.180
of the Ukrainian forces will depend

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.743
on how quickly they can learn.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.140
- Some of the Ukrainian armed forces

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.940
have operated tanks before

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.730
but most of them have not seen a tank.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.890
- [Narrator] But getting to
grips with battlefield tactics

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.530
and the electronic systems
on board could be difficult

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.240
for those without prior experience

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.220
according to defense analysts.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.200
The number of Western vehicles provided

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.480
could also be a hurdle for Ukraine.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.640
Kyiv requested 300 western tanks

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.830
but defense experts say only around 50

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.903
to 60 have been offered so far.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.380
Russian officials attacked
the pledges for tanks.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.410
Kremlin spokesman Dmitry
Peskov said Moscow sees them

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.716
as increasing the West's direct
involvement in the conflict.

00:04:37.716 --> 00:04:39.780
(soldiers shouting)

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.690
For the Ukrainian soldiers
training here in the UK,

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.235
the lessons could soon
be put into practice.

00:04:45.235 --> 00:04:47.902
(pensive music)

